# C++20 Coding Standards

## Format

- **Indentation:** 4 spaces, no tabs
- **Braces:** Allman style — opening brace on its own line
- **Naming:** `camelCase` (vars/functions), `PascalCase` (classes/structs), `_camelCase` (private members), `lowerCase` (namespaces)
- **Pointers/references:** align to type — `const Transform& t`, `SDL_Window* _window`
- **Extensions:** `.h` headers, `.cpp` implementations — no `.hpp`/`.hxx`

```cpp
void doSomething(int x)
{
    if (x > 0)
    {
        // ...
    }
}
```

## Code Practices

| Topic | Rule |
|-------|------|
| Headers vs `.cpp` | ≤3-line functions in `.h`; everything else in `.cpp` |
| `constexpr` | Use wherever value/computation is compile-time known |
| Classes | Only when state is needed; prefer free functions |
| RAII | Own resources in ctor/dtor; `unique_ptr`/`shared_ptr` for ownership; raw pointers for non-owning refs |
| Non-member fns | Prefer over member/friend when operating on a type |
| Structs | Plain public data for components — no methods |
| Enums | `enum class` outside classes; plain `enum` inside classes |
| Init | Value-init members with `{}`; designated initializers for aggregates |
| Headers | `#pragma once` only — no include guards |
| Exceptions | None — use `assert` for programmer errors, `std::expected`/error codes for recoverable failures |
| `optional` | Nullable returns/optional params — not as a pointer substitute |
| `final` / `= delete` | `final` when inheritance unintended; delete ctors on utility classes |

```cpp
// ✅ Component struct
struct Health
{
    int  points{};
    bool isInvulnerable{};
    bool isDead{};
};

// ✅ Utility system — no instantiation
class MovementSystem final : bagel::NoInstance {};

// ✅ Non-member over member
b2Vec2 transformToB2Pos(const Transform& t);

// ✅ Namespace — close with comment
namespace cafe
{
// ...
} // namespace cafe
```
